		<h3>CNN-Based Phase Imaging: A Quantitative Performance Analysis</h3>
		<p><em>University at Albany-State University of New York</em></p>
		<p>April 2024 – September 2025</p>
		<p>
			I worked on evaluating the performance of a convolutional neural network (CNN) for phase
			imaging, which is a technique used to visualize transparent samples. The CNN was trained to
			reconstruct phase images from intensity measurements, and I analyzed its performance using
			various metrics such as mean squared error, structural similarity index, and peak
			signal-to-noise ratio. I have attached a poster of my work, which I presented at the <a
				href="https://www.aps.org/events/2024/130th-symposium-aps-nyss"
				target="_blank"
				rel="noopener noreferrer">130th Topical Symposium of the APS New York State Section</a
			>.
		</p>
